# Build artefacts, not source.
#
# Three signed APKs, 161 MB between them. Git stores every version of a
# binary forever, so a rebuilt APK does not replace the old one — it is added
# next to it, and the clone gets slower for everybody permanently. Ship builds
# through releases or EAS, where they can be replaced and deleted.
apk-backup/
*.apk
*.aab

# Dependencies. Each project's own .gitignore covers its node_modules; this
# catches any that appear elsewhere.
node_modules/

# Secrets and machine-local configuration.
#
# The backend and admin .gitignore files already exclude their own .env — the
# backend's carries a live Atlas password and must never be committed. This
# adds the Expo app's, which was not covered: it holds no secret, but it
# points at http://localhost:4000, and committing one developer's machine as
# the API address breaks the app for everybody who clones it. .env.example is
# committed on purpose, so it is spared.
.env
!.env.example

# OS and editor noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
